# FATHOM
#
# Two jobs: keep build noise out, and make it hard for PII to reach history by accident.
# The PII sweep is the real gate (tools/pii_sweep.py); this is the belt to its braces.
#
# Note: git only treats '#' as a comment at the start of a line. No trailing comments on
# pattern lines — they become part of the pattern.

# --- Prime Directives 2.1: these must never be committed ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
.secrets/

# Encrypted operator store — stays on operator hardware
data/vault/

# Anything pre-redaction
data/raw/
**/raw/

# Raw call audio — 2.1, and 11.7 defaults the recorder to NO_AUDIO
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.aac
*.flac
*.ogg
*.mp4
*.mov

# Unredacted capture staging. Redacted artifacts live in the evidence store, not here.
screenshots/unredacted/
**/unredacted/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Node / UI ---
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
.next/

# --- Local databases and caches ---
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# out/ is tracked on purpose — it holds the submission deliverables (15).
.venv/
*.lock
